885362","description":"Jackson release 10/15/2013 this is at about 2500cfs Put in at the dam boated 13 miles. Top section is the best at this level","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Kurt Sisson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882673","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882673"}},{"id":"882675","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885364","description":"Last release of 6 for 2013  10/15/2013 ","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Kurt Sisson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882675","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882675"}},{"id":"883724","ext":"png","post_id":"886430","description":"Covington City Park boat ramp to Route 18/ Whitey's Boat Ramp.\r\n5 Minute video of 2.15 hour trip.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JMxuDxgAAvw","caption":"GoPro Recorded","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883724","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883724"}}],"detail":{"id":"1946","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"A class I-II run on clear, cold water, with optional II+ or III- rapids immediately below the dam (you can put on above or below them). This river, like some in the Commonwealth, has private property issues, although here related to fishing rather than access. According to the Blueway guide linked below, 'two stretches of river run through private property and are closed to fishing. Please respect private property and do not stop on shore or wade in the river.' However, that's not a problem for most boaters, and the public access points along the river are well developed and relatively frequent.\n\nTypical releases from the dam, around 200-250 cfs, are unfortunately too low for an enjoyable paddle. Approximately once per month on a Wednesday, late spring through early fall, there is a pulse release peaking around 3,500 cfs. See [Gathright Dam Releases](https://www.nao-wc.usace.army.mil/nao/projected_Q.html).\n\nSee Also:\n\n[Alleghany Highlands Blueway](https://visitalleghanyhighlands.com/uniquely-alleghany/alleghany-highlands-blueway/maps/) for maps and info.\n\n[Alleghany Outdoors](https://alleghanyoutdoors.com/) outfitters, Intervale Park.\n\n*Classic Virginia Rivers,* Ed Grove (1992 ed), p. 222.\n\n*Virginia Whitewater*, Roger Corbett (2000 ed.), p. 271.\n\n*Exploring Virginia's Waterways*, Ed Gertler (2022 ed.), p. 195.","averageGradient":"9","maxGradient":null,"length":"17","correlations":[{"reachID":"1946","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"350","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"10000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"JACKSON RIVER BL GATHRIGHT DAM NR HOT SPGS, VA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02011800","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"230","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"8.97","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"37.94845825","longitude":"-79.94922369"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/02011800","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02011800/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"230","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifie